// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! A USB class driver's two functions, after BeginIO and AbortIO: what
//! usb.library calls a driver in DEVS:usb/ with when it offers it an
//! interface, and when that interface goes. Every class driver has them
//! (sdk/devices/usbclass.zig); the base is the driver's, io_Device of an
//! open request.
##include libs/usb/usb as usb
##interface
##basetype UsbClassBase
##name usbclass
##bias 6
##public
/// An interface offered: true if the driver takes it - it has opened its
/// pipes and filled a unit, `binding.unit` saying which - false if it
/// declines and the next driver is asked. Called on the bus's process,
/// which nothing else on the bus moves while it runs: decide quickly,
/// and leave anything slow to the driver's own task. It may make control
/// transfers on the device (DoUSBControl) and open pipes.
bool USBClassBind(*usb.USBBinding binding)
/// The interface is gone - the device was pulled, or the bus stops: every
/// request the driver has outstanding on it answered, its pipes closed,
/// its unit left without what was in it. Called on the bus's process.
void USBClassUnbind(*usb.USBBinding binding)
##end
